# r1107cco boot 2: the same `full` srv and level cco1 rebooted with the toggled settings (scratch srv only):
#   srv/user_jvm_args.txt  -Dcreativecommon.iwFastTick=false                     (SQ-CCO-05 second half)
#   qrun.py toml srv/config/creativecommon-common.toml perf gravityLimitDimensions false   (SQ-CCO-08 second half)
#   qrun.py toml srv/config/creativecommon-common.toml effects removed '["minecraft:slowness"]'   (SQ-CCO-16 second half)
# SQ-CCO-08 samples the falling zombies every second: Gravity adds its modifier only while an entity falls.
pace 2

## SQ-CCO-05b | IW fast path off: the off line is logged and moss still spreads
bootexpect (?i)random-tick fast path off
bootreject (?i)unknown signature|handler not found
> pbot remove-all
sleep 2
> pbot spawn s5pb1 0 70 0 minecraft:overworld creative
> forceload add 0 0 31 31
> fill 8 69 8 23 69 23 minecraft:cobblestone
> fill 8 70 8 23 72 23 minecraft:air
> setblock 15 69 15 minecraft:mossy_cobblestone
> setblock 16 70 16 minecraft:water
> zq count 8 69 8 23 69 23 minecraft:mossy_cobblestone
> gamerule randomTickSpeed 300
sleep 60
> zq count 8 69 8 23 69 23 minecraft:mossy_cobblestone
> gamerule randomTickSpeed 3
look mossy_cobblestone count after 60 s is higher than the first count (growth without the fast path; compare with b2's 1 -> 83)

## SQ-CCO-08b | Create Gravity with gravityLimitDimensions = false (the mod's own behaviour): control for SQ-CCO-08
> kill @e[tag=cco08]
> execute in minecraft:the_end run forceload add 0 0
> time set 18000
> execute in minecraft:the_end run summon minecraft:zombie 0 200 0 {Silent:1b,PersistenceRequired:1b,Tags:["cco08","cco08e"]}
> execute in minecraft:overworld run summon minecraft:zombie 3 200 3 {Silent:1b,PersistenceRequired:1b,Tags:["cco08","cco08o"]}
pace 0
sleep 1
> execute in minecraft:the_end run data get entity @e[tag=cco08e,limit=1] Pos[1]
> data get entity @e[tag=cco08o,limit=1] Pos[1]
> execute in minecraft:the_end run data get entity @e[tag=cco08e,limit=1] Attributes
> data get entity @e[tag=cco08o,limit=1] Attributes
sleep 1
> execute in minecraft:the_end run data get entity @e[tag=cco08e,limit=1] Pos[1]
> data get entity @e[tag=cco08o,limit=1] Pos[1]
pace 2
> kill @e[tag=cco08]
> time set noon
look with Common's limit off: does the End zombie fall slower / carry the Low Gravity Biome modifier? If not, Gravity itself does not apply it here and SQ-CCO-08's End half cannot show Common's effect

## SQ-CCO-16b | [effects] removed = ["minecraft:slowness"]: Slowness refused, Speed applies
> effect give s5pb1 minecraft:slowness 30 0
> effect give s5pb1 minecraft:speed 30 0
> data get entity s5pb1 ActiveEffects
expect Applied effect Speed to s5pb1
reject "minecraft:slowness"|Id: 2b
> pbot remove-all
look ActiveEffects holds Speed and no Slowness (the give line for Slowness may say it could not be applied)
